38:15.490 --> 38:18.970
Wednesdays. So that way we can still make sure that those notices of

38:19.470 --> 38:22.810
motion get on the agenda when it's released. As I noted, we've removed the

38:23.310 --> 38:27.050
differences in rules of procedure for committees and council. So now

38:27.550 --> 38:31.210
there is no reason on council nights to have

38:31.710 --> 38:34.782
motions to go into committee the whole and to rise and resume. It's just a

38:35.282 --> 38:36.750
formality at this point. So we're recommending that that be removed from the required order

38:37.250 --> 38:40.563
of agenda. And we're codifying that a councillor may correct their vote

38:41.063 --> 38:42.830
up to the point that the results of the vote are declared, and at which

38:43.330 --> 38:46.710
point a change can only be made with the unanimous consent of the council.

38:47.210 --> 38:52.030
There are a few others in there and they're outlined in

38:52.270 --> 38:55.910
appendix A. Council, should the recommendation be approved today, staff will

38:56.410 --> 39:00.160
